  "request": "GET /api/requirements/export?project_idx=1&*",
  "body": {
   "content": "# What this project must keep doing, kept beside its code (cloop requirements).\n#\n# Review changes here like code. `cloop requirements import` brings them into the\n# hub, `cloop requirements export` writes the hub's back, and\n# `cloop requirements check --file .cloop/requirements.yaml` runs the approved\n# requirements' tests without a hub. An id is never given to a second\n# requirement. Format: docs/guides/requirements.md#requirements-as-code\n\nversion: 1\nrequirements:\n  - id: R-1\n    title: The hero names the product and offers a sign-up button\n    status: approved\n    priority: must\n    details: Visitors see what Tidewater is and can start straight away.\n    tests:\n      - name: hero has a sign-up button\n        command: grep -q 'id=\"signup\"' index.html\n        timeout: 30s\n  - id: R-2\n    title: Every in-page link points at a section that exists\n    status: approved\n    priority: must\n    details: 'No dead #anchors in the navigation or the buttons.'\n    tests:\n      - name: in-page links resolve\n        command: sh tests/links.sh\n        timeout: 30s\n  - id: R-3\n    title: The page loads no third-party scripts\n    status: approved\n    priority: must\n    details: Nothing is fetched from another origin when the page loads.\n    tests:\n      - name: no remote scripts\n        command: '! grep -Eq ''<script[^>]+src=\"https?://'' index.html'\n        timeout: 30s\n  - id: R-4\n    title: Search engines get a description of the page\n    status: approved\n    priority: should\n    details: A meta description of at most 160 characters.\n    tests:\n      - name: meta description present\n        command: grep -q '<meta name=\"description\"' index.html\n        timeout: 30s\n",
   "ok": true,
   "path": ".cloop/requirements.yaml",
   "requirements": 4,
   "sha256": "120a8349bd558f6bea369dec78a8dcd7851beff820251ec370045e49d12c1ddd"
  }
